{"packet_id":"D027-01","doc_id":"D027","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Aggregate income standard for co-applicants","requirement":"A landlord may not use a financial or income standard in renting housing that fails to account for the aggregate income of persons who live or propose to live together on the same basis as married persons living together.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"The rental of any housing accommodation; the text sets no limits by unit count, building age, or owner type.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"All housing accommodations in the rental of housing"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2024-01-01","citation":"Cal. Gov. Code § 12955","quoted_span":"(n) To use a financial or income standard in the rental of housing that fails to account for the aggregate income of persons residing together or proposing to reside together on the same basis as the aggregate income of married persons residing together or proposing to reside together.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D027-01","doc_id":"D027","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Screening limits for applicants with a government rent subsidy","requirement":"When there is a government rent subsidy, a landlord may not use an income standard not based on the tenant's share of rent, and may not use credit history without offering the applicant the option to provide lawful, verifiable alternative evidence of ability to pay.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Applies where there is a government rent subsidy; the provision does not limit requesting employment information, landlord references, or identity verification.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Rentals with a government rent subsidy"},"exemptions":"Does not limit the owner's ability to request information or documentation to verify employment, to request landlord references, or to verify the identity of a person.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2024-01-01","citation":"Cal. Gov. Code § 12955","quoted_span":"(o) (1) In instances in which there is a government rent subsidy, to do either of the following: (A) Use a financial or income standard in assessing eligibility for the rental of housing that is not based on the portion of the rent to be paid by the tenant. (B) (i) Use a person’s credit history as part of the application process for a rental accommodation without offering the applicant the option, at the applicant’s discretion, of providing lawful, verifiable alternative evidence of the applicant’s reasonable ability to pay the portion of the rent to be paid by the tenant, including, but not limited to, government benefit payments, pay records, and bank statements.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D027-01","doc_id":"D027","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Source of income includes housing vouchers","requirement":"Source of income under the housing discrimination ban means lawful, verifiable income, including public assistance and federal, state, or local housing subsidies such as Section 8 vouchers; asking about income level or source is not itself discrimination.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Housing accommodations covered by this section's discrimination ban; source of income includes Section 8 and HUD-VASH vouchers.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"All housing accommodations covered by the section"},"exemptions":"A housing owner or landlord is not a tenant's representative unless the source of income is a HUD-VASH voucher; written or oral inquiry about the level or source of income is not discrimination.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2024-01-01","citation":"Cal. Gov. Code § 12955","quoted_span":"For the purposes of this section, “source of income” means lawful, verifiable income paid directly to a tenant, or to a representative of a tenant, or paid to a housing owner or landlord on behalf of a tenant, including federal, state, or local public assistance, and federal, state, or local housing subsidies, including, but not limited to, federal housing assistance vouchers issued under Section 8 of the United States Housing Act of 1937 (42 U.S.C. Sec. 1437f).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
